msgid "The rest of the stack"
msgstr "栈中的其余部分"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "Because everything is a Quarkus extension, a lot of what would normally be infrastructure work was configuration:"
msgstr "由于一切都是 Quarkus 扩展，因此许多原本属于基础架构的工作都变成了配置："

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache` + `quarkus-jdbc-oracle`** against the existing Oracle schema, with a snake-case physical naming strategy so the Java entities read like Java and the tables stay as the ERP defined them decades ago."
msgstr "*quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache+quarkus-jdbc-oracle* 基于现有的 Oracle 模式，采用蛇形命名法作为物理命名策略，这样 Java 实体名称读起来像 Java 代码，而表名则保持数十年前 ERP 定义时的原样。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-cache`** and the Hibernate second-level cache for reference data — aircraft master, locations, gates, profiles — warmed at startup and invalidated by the CDC handlers. Reference data that changes twice a year should not be a database round trip on every request."
msgstr "*quarkus-cache* 以及用于参考数据（飞机主数据、位置、登机口、配置文件）的 Hibernate 二级缓存——在启动时预热，并由 CDC 处理程序进行失效操作。每年仅更新两次的参考数据，不应在每次请求时都进行数据库往返操作。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-oidc`** with Keycloak, mapping OIDC token claims onto the fine-grained permissions already modeled in the ERP."
msgstr "*quarkus-oidc* 与 Keycloak 配合使用，将 OIDC 令牌声明映射到 ERP 中已建模的细粒度权限上。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-micrometer-opentelemetry`** and **`quarkus-micrometer-registry-prometheus`**, pointed at a Grafana LGTM stack. JDBC telemetry, scheduler metrics and WebSocket metrics are all one property each."
msgstr "*quarkus-micrometer-opentelemetry* 和 *quarkus-micrometer-registry-prometheus，* 指向一个 Grafana LGTM 堆栈。JDBC 遥测、调度器指标和 WebSocket 指标各占一个属性。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-scheduler`**, **`quarkus-qute`**, **`quarkus-amazon-s3`** and a couple of Quarkiverse PDF extensions for the reporting and document side."
msgstr "*quarkus-scheduler* 、 *quarkus-qute* 、 *quarkus-amazon-s3* 以及几个用于报表和文档处理的 Quarkiverse PDF 扩展。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "**`quarkus-smallrye-health`** and **`quarkus-info`** so the platform team gets liveness, readiness and build metadata without us writing an endpoint."
msgstr "*quarkus-smallrye-health* 和 *quarkus-info* ，这样平台团队就能获取系统运行状态、就绪状态和构建元数据，而无需我们编写端点。"

msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "解决方案"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid "The thing that stands out to me about this project is how *little* of it is plumbing."
msgstr "这个项目最让我印象深刻的一点是，其中涉及的水管工程部分 *非常少* 。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The hard parts of the problem are genuinely hard: capturing changes from an Oracle database you do not exclusively own, getting them to a mechanic's iPad reliably enough that they trust it, and keeping two independently-built front ends in lockstep with a Java API.\n"
"But the code that solves those problems is a topology producer, a handful of handler classes, one annotated WebSocket endpoint and a build property that writes an OpenAPI file to disk."
msgstr "该问题的难点确实很难解决：从一个并非由你独家拥有的 Oracle 数据库中捕获变更，将这些变更可靠地传输到维修技师的 iPad 上，使其能够信任这些数据，并确保两个独立开发的前端通过 Java API 保持步调一致。 但解决这些问题的代码其实很简单：一个拓扑生成器、几个处理程序类、一个带注解的 WebSocket 端点，以及一个将 OpenAPI 文件写入磁盘的构建属性。"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kafka Streams, WebSockets, CDI events, OIDC, OpenTelemetry, Oracle and OpenAPI are one dependency each and one consistent configuration file, and they all show up together in Dev UI when something is not behaving.\n"
"That is the Quarkus pitch, and on this project it held up."
msgstr "Kafka Streams、WebSockets、CDI 事件、OIDC、OpenTelemetry、Oracle 和 OpenAPI 各占一个依赖项，且仅需一个统一的配置文件，当系统出现异常时，这些组件都会在开发界面中同时显示出来。这就是 Quarkus 的卖点，而在本项目中，这一优势得到了充分验证。"
